      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Short answer: No? (I personally wouldn't want iOS or Android support abandoned in favor of VCC.)\n\nLonger answer: https://github.com/vrchat-community/creator-companion/issues\n\nVRChat Creator Companion may as well be abandonware now, because [VCC only supports Windows 10](https://feedback.vrchat.com/creator-companion/p/please-support-the-latest-windows-version-windows-11-windows-10-support-has-ende) - and [Windows 10 support has ended on October 14, 2025](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/windows-10-support-has-ended-on-october-14-2025-2ca8b313-1946-43d3-b55c-2b95b107f281).\n\n[ALCOM](https://vrc-get.anatawa12.com/en/alcom/) isn't abandonware at this time, and supports GNU/Linux and does what VCC would do.",
